MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink doorbell feels like a useful next purchase because it connects my earlier interest in home security with the Alexa devices I already use.",
    "Echo Auto offers a new use for Alexa, and a larger Echo Show has some appeal. The memory card also fits my storage-accessory history, though those interests do not mean I need them now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The older Echo Dot and Echo Show 5 duplicate devices I already own in newer versions. Buying a stand for my current Show 5 suggests I am continuing to use it.",
    "Desktop memory and an internal SSD assume an upgrade project I have not shown interest in. Charging cables and a headphone adapter likewise require a specific need or compatible device that my history does not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated Alexa purchases seem to be taken as interest in any Echo device, even when it would repeat something I already have.",
    "My purchases of practical computer accessories seem to be treated as interest in unrelated accessories and internal components, regardless of what problem they would solve."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent device generations and purchases of matching accessories matter: I want something that adds a useful capability rather than an older replacement.",
    "My purchases often serve a concrete task, such as connecting devices, maintaining equipment, or adding external storage. Compatibility and a current need matter more than broad resemblance to past purchases."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in Alexa and practical electronics, but miss the difference between a useful addition, a redundant device, and an accessory I have no reason to buy now."
}
